<Layout title="About">
  <Textcontainer
    heading="About"
    image="/images/KellyeDanSuitScan.png"
    imageAlt="Kellye Coffyn, owner and designer of Long Time Gone"
    imageUrl="https://www.dsdphoto.co.uk"
  >
    LongTimeGone creates bespoke Western Wear using traditional techniques.
    <br />
    <br />
    Beginning with hand-embroidered Western wear in 2017, owner, designer and stitcher
    KellyeSue Coffyn brought the styles of her native Texas to the UK, inspired by
    country music culture, the embroidered suits worn by performers like Dolly Parton
    and Hank Williams, and the beautiful natural surroundings of her adopted home
    of Yorkshire.
    <br /><br />

    Kellye worked as a tailor and embroiderer for the legneday Maneul Cuevas in
    Nashville, Tennessee - making embroidered rhinestoned suits for country
    music royalty. She trained in traditional British bespoke tailoring and
    pattern cutting techniques at the Tailoring Academy, and has a Level 5
    diploma in Bespoke Tailoring and Cutting.

    <br /><br />Every design is hand drawn and each stitch positioned by hand -
    nothing is computerised, digitised or mass produced. Before LTG, Kellye
    spent nearly 20 years in academia, primarily as a research physicist.

   
    <br /><br /> The embroidery machines are antiques and operated in the traditional
    ways, same as on the suits worn by Gram Parsons, George Jones, Loretta Lynn, and
    on and on. Having had a love for textile arts and making clothing since childhood,
    as well as a fascination with tinkering with machines, she now combines the cowboy
    aesthetics of her youth with her analytical training and precise attention to
    detail to create beautiful, one-of-a-kind wearable works of art.
    <br /><br />
    <Textcontainer
      image="/images/livechainstitchDan.jpg"
      imageAlt="Kellye Coffyn, owner and designer of Long Time Gone"
      imageUrl="https://www.dsdphoto.co.uk"
    />
    To find out more about the process of creating a bespoke garment, visit the <a href="/bespoke">Bespoke</a> page.  

     <br /><br />
    With LongTimeGone, sustainability is a main priority, and deadstock materials
    and vintage fabrics are used to help ensure your one-of-a-kind garment is also
    kind to the earth.
  </Textcontainer>
</Layout>
